    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_08c3eadcb039d38b430aa1d79965eff5c33eea0f1339e76ec5719f7156092926",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Source fact: for independent centered Gaussian or symmetric uniformly bounded coefficients, square-summable sup norms of coefficient functions and first derivatives give almost-sure uniform convergence and exponential sup-norm bounds; all-derivative summability gives a C-infinity limit and exponential C^ell control, including partial-sum oscillations. Interpretation: termwise variance summability is converted into pathwise function-space regularity and quantitative tails, supplying reusable control for later error fields. Boundary: independence, centering or symmetry, bounded/Gaussian concentration, and derivative summability are essential; smoothness does not imply analyticity.",
