    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_0bcf66ee81bc7ca558041ae5043e7bfc4000d662db8e3c20d5546fb914c6c3b6",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The prime-indexed Gaussian field is first converted, through three separately controlled replacements, into a Brownian integral with logarithmic-frequency weight u^{-1/2} plus a smooth error. After dilation, splitting that spectral integral at delta and 1 separates a spatially constant Gaussian contribution with variance log(1/delta) from centered low-frequency increments and the remaining spatial chaos, whose law is independent of delta. Quotienting by nonzero scalars removes exactly the divergent constant factor and leaves the stable chaos shape.",
