    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_346bc1806993aeca7df795d99b29a7e16d46926250f35379646c01dc0675d833",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The Haar model reaches Gaussian chaos through a front end different from the zeta model: determinant moments together with Fisher-Hartwig and strong Szego asymptotics control truncation, and fixed trace vectors converge to independent Gaussian logarithmic modes. The mesoscopic argument then dilates that global boundary field, factors only the constant parts of low modes, retains their centered spatial increments, and couples all discrete modes to the Brownian field eta. This proves that the model-specific global controls feed a common mesoscopic chaos after the divergent scalar is separated.",
